 to membranes during nucleotide-evoked exocytosis.</article-title><source>J Cell Sci</source><volume>115</volume><fpage>3909</fpage><lpage>3922</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12244129</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004841-Ikeda1"><label>26</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ikeda</surname><given-names>SR</given-names></name></person-group><year>1991</year><article-title>Double-pulse calcium channel current facilitation in adult rat sympathetic neurones.</article-title><source>J Physiol</source><volume>439</volume><fpage>181</fpage><lpage>214</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1654413</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004841-Scamps1"><label>27</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Scamps</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Valentin</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Dayanithi</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Valmier</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><year>1998</year><article-title>Calcium channel subtypes responsible for voltage-gated intracellular calcium elevations in embryonic rat motoneurons.</article-title><source>Neuroscience</source><volume>87</volume><fpage>719</fpage><lpage>730</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9758236</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004841-Schnee1"><label>28</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Schnee</surname><given-names>ME</given-names></name><name><surname>Ricci</surname><given-names>AJ</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Biophysical and pharmacological characterization of voltage-gated calcium currents in turtle auditory hair cells.</article-title><source>J Physiol</source><volume>549</volume><fpage>697</fpage><lpage>717</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12740421</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.00048